    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a0c9ec37959bbb613b98af180f34e31e85c4579100c513c3c0210acc60299c21",
      "text": "Day 6 · To Alta Verapaz, the greenest and rainiest region of Guatemala (about 3 hours). Near Cobán, the Quetzal Biotope protects the resplendent quetzal, sacred to the ancient Maya and now a national symbol of Guatemala: walk its trails through humid cloud forest among orchids, ferns and bromeliads, watching for hummingbirds and toucans, and, with luck, a quetzal. Continue to Lanquín (about 4 hours) for a glamping night in comfortable, well-equipped tents. (B)",
